<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Tucumán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of Tucumán was the assembly of deputies from the United Provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> that met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-miguel-de-tucuman">San Miguel de Tucumán</a> from March 1816. On 9 July 1816 it declared independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, a date now celebrated as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>'s Independence Day. The congress later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, where it adopted a centralist constitution in 1819 that the provinces rejected.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-tucuman.jpg" alt="Congress of Tucumán" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Angel Paganelli (1832-1928) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casa_de_Tucum%C3%A1n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
